# Single source of truth for the toolchain this repo is *built with* (not the version it is
# released as - that one lives in gyllir.toml). Sourced by every CI workflow and by the
# Dockerfile invocation documented at the top of ./Dockerfile.
#
# - YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION / GCC_VERSION: the prebuilt `gyc` release used to compile ymirc,
#   published as a .deb by github.com/GNU-Ymir/gymir (release tag = YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION,
#   asset = gyc-<GCC major>_<YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION>_amd64.deb - only the GCC *major* appears
#   in the asset name).
# - GYLLIR_VERSION: the `gyllir` build tool release used to drive that compiler, published by
#   github.com/GNU-Ymir/Gyllir (release tag = GYLLIR_VERSION, asset =
#   gyllir_<GYLLIR_VERSION>_amd64.deb).
# - MIDGARD_VERSION: the standard library (midgard) sources the *test suite* compiles against,
#   published by github.com/GNU-Ymir/yruntime (release tag = MIDGARD_VERSION, asset =
#   midgard-<MIDGARD_VERSION>-src.zip). The gyc .deb only ships the stdlib matching its own
#   version, while ymirc looks for /usr/include/ymir/<ymirc::global::common::MIDGARD_VERSION>
#   (major.minor of the line below), so these sources are installed there separately - see
#   ./Dockerfile. Both that constant and __YMIR_VERSION__ in common.yr are rewritten from this
#   file and gyllir.toml by tools/set-version.sh, run as a pre-build command (see gyllir.toml).
YMIR_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION=1.3.2
GCC_VERSION=15.3.1
GYLLIR_VERSION=1.6.3
MIDGARD_VERSION=1.3.6
